  PASS  non-fast-forward on a branch the policy does not open (refused, as the policy says)
  PASS  and the branch did not move
  PASS  force where the policy allows it
  PASS  --force-with-lease against the ref the client last saw
  PASS  --force-with-lease with a stale expectation is refused (refused, as the policy says)
  PASS  the control: without --atomic the good half of the pair lands
  PASS  push --atomic: one bad ref and NEITHER lands
  PASS  push -o reaches the server
  PASS  push --all
  PASS  concurrent pushes to different branches both land

== names the protocol allows ==
  PASS  a ref with slashes
  PASS  a long ref name
  PASS  a UTF-8 ref name

== the repository the server hands back is whole ==
  PASS  a final clone matches the working tree's tip and passes fsck --strict
  PASS  and the bucket alone rebuilds the same tip

